Self (archive footage), played by Ayrton Senna.

5
00:31:10,588 --> 00:31:16,588
Self, played by Alain Prost.

6
00:37:24,705 --> 00:37:30,705
Self, played by Frank Williams.

7
00:43:38,823 --> 00:43:44,823
Self, played by Ron Dennis.

8
00:49:52,941 --> 00:49:58,941
Self, played by Viviane Senna.

9
00:56:07,058 --> 00:56:13,058
Self (archive footage), played by Milton da Silva.

10
01:02:21,176 --> 01:02:27,176
Senna is a 2010 documentary film that depicts the life and death of Brazilian
motor-racing champion Ayrton Senna, directed by Asif Kapadia.

11
01:08:35,294 --> 01:08:41,294
The film was produced by StudioCanal, Working Title Films, and Midfield Films, and was distributed
by the parent company of the latter two production companies, Universal Pictures.

12
01:14:49,411 --> 01:14:55,411
The film's narrative focuses on Senna's racing career in Formula One, from his debut in the 1984 Brazilian Grand Prix to his death in
an accident at the 1994 San Marino Grand Prix, with particular emphasis on his rivalry with fellow driver Alain Prost.

13
01:21:03,529 --> 01:21:09,529
Unlike a traditional documentary, it has no formal commentary or retrospective "talking head" interviews, and relies primarily on
archival racetrack and broadcast news footage, voiceover narration, and home video clips provided by the Senna family.

14
01:27:17,647 --> 01:27:23,647
Senna was acclaimed by critics.

15
01:33:31,764 --> 01:33:37,764
At the 65th British Academy Film Awards, it won two BAFTAs for Best Documentary and Best
Editing, and also received a nomination for Outstanding British Film.

16
01:39:45,882 --> 01:39:51,882
The film explores themes of sports car,
competition, champion, biography, rivalry.
